# Architecture

Dependency direction is one-way and lint-enforced:

    actions → services → repositories/providers → mappers/schemas/policies/types/constants

Containers and hooks sit on the view side and reach services only through server
actions. Components receive computed props and return TSX — no state, no data
access, no logic. Nothing below the view layer imports React.

Cross-module imports go through a declared surface: index, server, client,
dashboard, ingestion-ui, editor-ui, account-ui. A deep import into another
module's directories is an error.

Implementation files do not declare module-level types, interfaces, enums or
non-function constants. Those live in types/, enums/ and constants/.
